<title>USA: W. Virginia jobless rate climbs to 8.3 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>W. Virginia jobless rate climbs to 8.3 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLESTON, W.Va. 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Virginia's unemployment rate jumped to 8.3 percent in January from 7.5 percent in December, state labor officials said Monday.</p>
<p>Calhoun County had the state's highest unemployment rate, 22 percent, leading for the third consecutive month. Pendleton and Jefferson counties had the lowest rate, at 4.8 percent.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
